# Instructor preparation

## Status

This website is a teaching adaptation, not a verbatim copy of the
original scripts.

Test the entire practical using the exact teaching files and software
versions before publishing it for students.

The course contains no PRS lesson.

## 1. Download the upstream material

```bash
mkdir -p upstream
git clone https://github.com/MareesAT/GWA_tutorial.git upstream/GWA_tutorial

git -C upstream/GWA_tutorial rev-parse HEAD \
  > upstream/repository_commit.txt

cd upstream/GWA_tutorial

unzip 1_QC_GWAS.zip
unzip 2_Population_stratification.zip
unzip 3_Association_GWAS.zip
```

Inspect and test the main scripts before class.

Do not assume that historical external download addresses still work.

## 2. Prepare the classroom input

Create:

```text
Course_Materials/
├── Data/raw/
├── Data/review/
├── Results/
└── scripts/
```

From the first original module, identify the unfiltered binary dataset
that includes the intended simulated case/control phenotype.

Do not substitute the final QC output for the initial dataset:
students are expected to perform the filtering exercises themselves.

Export the chosen input with the standardized prefix:

```bash
plink \
  --bfile /actual/path/to/verified_input_prefix \
  --make-bed \
  --out /actual/path/to/Course_Materials/Data/raw/study
```

Verify:

- Dataset provenance.
- Phenotype coding.
- Sample identifiers.
- Variant identifiers.
- Chromosome coding.
- Genome build.
- Presence and treatment of sex-chromosome markers.

Record these details in a data manifest distributed with the course.

The paths above are placeholders that must be replaced.

## 3. Prepare sample-review material

Run the classroom variant-filtering steps before preparing review lists.

Use the original module's sample-QC procedures, including the necessary
sex-chromosome preparation.

Prepare:

- Sex-chromosome diagnostic results.
- Heterozygosity diagnostics.
- Relatedness diagnostics.
- Written reasons for exclusions or retention.

Create:

```text
Data/review/qc_exclusions.txt
Data/review/review_notes.tsv
```

The exclusion file must contain two whitespace-separated columns,
FID and IID, without a header.

Use an empty file if no exclusion is justified.

Suggested review-notes columns:

```text
FID IID diagnostic evidence decision reason
```

These are reviewed classroom decisions, not fabricated examples.

For a more advanced class, have students propose decisions before
revealing the instructor list.

## 4. Prepare the population-structure component

Test the original second module with its reference data.

Verify genome-build and allele compatibility before merging.

Prepare a reference-based plot with clearly identified study and
reference samples.

Document the marker set and all harmonization decisions.

Create:

```text
Data/review/population_exclusions.txt
```

Use the same two-column, no-header format.

If no exclusions are justified, distribute an empty file.

The main classroom association dataset must contain only retained study
participants, not reference individuals.

## 5. Decide how students access the reference exercise

Choose one:

### Full practical

Students execute the tested reference workflow in the original second
module before returning to Section 5.3 of the website.

Distribute a version-specific command sheet with verified paths.

### Short practical

Provide the reference plot, selected diagnostic outputs, and review
notes. Students interpret the evidence without downloading and merging
the complete reference data during class.

State clearly which version the class is using.

## 6. Validate the complete lesson

Run every completed exercise from a clean working directory.

Check:

- All referenced input files exist.
- Identifier fields remain unchanged.
- Cases and controls remain after filtering.
- Covariates match the retained samples.
- MDS dimensions can be calculated.
- Adjusted and unadjusted models use comparable samples.
- Failed regressions are identified.
- All plots are generated.
- Empty exclusion lists are handled correctly.

Save expected sample and variant counts for your exact course release.

Do not invent expected association hits: use the output of the tested
teaching dataset.

## 7. Public repository content

Publish:

- Lesson text.
- Website configuration.
- Original teaching scripts.
- Non-sensitive illustrative figures, where permitted.
- Dataset provenance and access instructions.

Keep working genotype data, sample-level reports, and upstream
downloads outside the public teaching repository unless redistribution
is explicitly appropriate and permitted.

Retain attribution for third-party materials. Check their terms before
redistributing them; do not assume your repository's license applies
to upstream content.
